WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:07.000
If an underground organism of unfathomable
size were unearthed in the United States,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.180
you might expect widespread panic at the horrifying
discovery — or expect the U.S. government

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.309
to block off the cosmic terror from civilians.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:20.100
You might not expect the entity to be turned
into a theme park marketed towards all ages.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.890
But that’s what happened with the (thankfully)
fictional “Mystery Flesh Pit National Park,”

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:30.910
the name given to a creature of indeterminate
size and origin that was nonetheless turned

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:32.489
into a tourist attraction.

00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:38.590
"Mystery Flesh Pit” is an ongoing multimedia
narrative project by the creator Trevor Roberts,

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:41.230
who you can follow and support in the links
below.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:46.870
The story of the pit is told through fliers,
advertisements, and posters that rebrand the

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.420
horrifying lifeform as a relaxing family getaway.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:55.420
It’s this upbeat language around something
so blatantly terrifying that makes The Mystery

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.750
Flesh Pit so amusing… and so unsettling.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.770
Just the sort of thing to cover at this spooky
time of year.

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:07.330
But since venturing into the darkness of an
unknown organism is a little frightening to

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.700
do on one’s own, E.D.G.E. will be joining
me for this entry.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.970
He makes great content about Prehistoric life,
unique modern animals, and bizarre cryptids,

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:20.080
so he’s just the person to help investigate
this mysterious organism.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.730
Now, let’s begin our descent…

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:29.710
Unearthed accidentally in the early 1970s,
The Mystery Flesh Pit, also known as the Permian

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:34.479
Basin Superorganism, is located in West Texas.

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:39.780
Discovered by oil workers, the first tours
of the pit were given by James Jackson — a

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.740
small-time oilman and showman.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:48.510
The Mystery Flesh Pit was then further studied
and reinforced by Anodyne Inc, a deep mining

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:55.369
corporation who opened the park as a tourist
attraction in 1976 with assurances it was

00:01:55.369 --> 00:01:57.050
perfectly safe.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.350
We know how corporations are.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:04.660
In selling the park to the public, Anodyne
downplayed the horrifying nature of the pit

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:11.160
itself, creating a friendly cartoon mascot,
Caver Coop, who assured families the pit was

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:13.230
nothing to be afraid of.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:19.180
The attraction was later absorbed into the
National Park System in the early 1980s, which

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:24.230
led to the Permian Basin Superorganism becoming
further normalized.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:29.650
Surprising absolutely no one, thousands of
tourists regularly exploring the inside of

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:36.780
an unknown organism would eventually prove
to be a bad idea, as the infamous 2007 disaster

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.610
would prove, but that’s a story we’ll
get to later…

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:44.920
For now, let’s try to piece together the
material the author has given us to try and

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.300
understand the Pit’s Biology.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:52.519
Like many aspects of the pit, the more visceral
reality of the organism was glossed over with

00:02:52.519 --> 00:02:56.300
clinical language by the professionals who
studied it.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:01.629
Since an organism of this size defied conventional
science, numerous new disciplines were founded

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:03.240
to understand it.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:08.380
Geobiology is the term used for how the organism
interacts with its environment.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:13.230
Looking at this early map, you can see the
lifeform possesses musculoskeletal, nervous,

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:18.920
limbic, and vascular systems similar to traditional
life — at least on the top layer.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:26.099
This section of the pit is only a small fragment
of a larger, more complex organism.

00:03:26.099 --> 00:03:27.130
How large?

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:32.129
Data collected from a series of boreholes
shown in this diagram suggests that in some

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:36.900
places, the organism extends over 30 kilometers
below the earth’s surface.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:41.239
For reference, the Marianas trench is only
11 kilometers deep.

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:46.230
Indeed, the author suggests that the pit may
well extend into the earth’s mantle, with

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:51.080
some imaginary scientists suggesting that
the organism may be native to the interior

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:57.130
of the planet, having merely “surfaced”
to the upper tectonic plates for unknown reasons.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:01.769
And despite public assurances to the contrary,
there’s evidence that people working behind

00:04:01.769 --> 00:04:05.530
the scenes long understood the superorganism
to be dangerous.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:10.590
At one point in this fictional alternate history,
the U.S. government launched an investigation

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:14.950
into the feasibility of using nuclear weapons
to kill the lifeform.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:19.370
Although only the cover of this report was
ever photographed, the conclusion seemed to

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:22.079
be a resounding “no.”

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:26.580
What made the Permian Basin Superorganism
so potentially catastrophic?

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:30.210
The answers may lie deeper within...

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:36.000
In the early days of the Pit, a mission called
Project Freefall was planned to chart the

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.240
organism to a greater depth than ever before.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:44.150
A joint effort between the U.S. government
and Russian scientists, the expedition involved

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:49.240
a six-person team lowered into the pit via
specialized vehicle.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:55.530
Over a period of two weeks, the pod descended
down the dark wet skooshy pit, reaching regions

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:58.270
that had never been explored before.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:04.020
At last, the probe drilled through a dense
layer of lower cartilage and entered an unknown

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.199
region of ‘blue tissue.’

00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:09.290
A single person pod was lowered into this
opening.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:14.160
The Russian pilot described a ‘reflective’
and ‘prismatic’ environment — of which

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:19.100
we only have a single image from this onboard
computer.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:25.320
When the pod was raised back to the surface,
it was heavily damaged, and the pilot was

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:26.320
missing.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:32.720
The researchers concluded an attack from an
unknown organism was the likely cause.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:37.880
Project Freefall makes it clear that the organic
section of the Mystery Flesh Pit is merely

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:44.020
a portion of the lifeform, and other regions
are unlike anything in the natural world.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:47.690
It also made it clear people aren’t alone
in the pit…

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:52.380
Even above the deeper layers, which weren’t
available to the public, hostile wildlife

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.009
was frequently encountered.

00:05:54.009 --> 00:06:00.240
Large, crustacean-like organisms were spotted
as early as the first explorations, as this

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.870
sketch shows.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:07.060
In typical Mystery Flesh Pit fashion, however,
the corporate higher ups turned these terrifying

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:09.889
lifeforms into part of the marketing.

00:06:09.889 --> 00:06:14.780
Wildlife safety brochures were handed out
to visitors, explaining the exciting ‘anatomical

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:18.500
fauna’ that dwelled in the pit, and how
to avoid getting eaten.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:23.140
At the foundation of the pit’s ecosystem,
playing a role similar to bacteria in the

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:27.030
bodies of regular-sized animals, were macrobacteria.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:32.830
Unlike tiny bacteria you can only spot under
a microscope, Macrobacteria were multicellular

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:37.820
goliaths that could reach lengths of 12 feet,
or 4 meters across.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:43.330
This educational chart produced by the Park
Service showcases the various types of macrobacteria

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:49.080
— and the other bizarre species that dwell
in this imaginary Permian Basin Superorganism.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:54.360
We won’t be able to cover them all, but
one notable species is the Mesogleal Tridecapod,

00:06:54.360 --> 00:07:00.340
an insect-like species that gets its name
from its thirteen legs — as this faded ‘Wild

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:03.160
About Nature’ infographic will tell you.

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:07.870
These pseudo-vertebrates are almost the size
of humans, and aren’t technically vampires

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:10.039
as this guide will assure you…

00:07:10.039 --> 00:07:14.289
although they do feed off the pit and look
like something out of my nightmares.

00:07:14.289 --> 00:07:19.440
In other areas of the pit, there were sightings
of other, more dangerous species — and even

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:25.610
rumors of human-like lifeforms called ‘marrow
folk’… which Anodyne Inc strongly denied.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:30.860
They maintained the Mystery Flesh Pit was
just like any other national park, and anyone

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:35.650
who mysteriously vanished just didn’t read
their brochure carefully enough.

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:41.580
With the Permian Basin Superorganism so hostile
to human life, excavating it was a challenge

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:45.990
— a challenge that began with finding people
to staff it.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:51.300
As this oddly hilarious park ranger recruitment
bulletin suggests, however, with the right

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:56.970
benefits and incentives, Anodyne Inc. was
in fact able to find people willing to enlist

00:07:56.970 --> 00:08:00.340
in the Mystery Flesh Pit park ranger program.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:02.430
What kinds of jobs did this entail?

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:05.610
Well, why not become a Park Trail Engineer?

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:11.419
This anxiety producing position involved using
compact ‘stent-frames’ and other highly

00:08:11.419 --> 00:08:15.699
specialized tools to create new pathways within
the Pit.

00:08:15.699 --> 00:08:22.389
To be a Park Trail Engineer required extensive
knowledge of caving, geology, and macrobiology

00:08:22.389 --> 00:08:26.629
— as attacks from local wildlife were apparently
common.

00:08:26.629 --> 00:08:32.810
For personal protection, the LaserScope “Anatomical
Environment Multitool” was the most reliable

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:34.029
defense.

00:08:34.029 --> 00:08:39.300
Intended to blast new paths within the Mystery
Flesh Pit, this portable tool — an example

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:45.160
of which is on display here — was frequently
used to ward off aggressive lifeforms.

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:51.529
To more safely traverse the Pit’s interior,
Anodyne Inc. developed the Internal Anatomy

00:08:51.529 --> 00:08:56.959
Vehicle, or IAV: a vehicle that could traverse
the slickest and steepest of routes, which

00:08:56.959 --> 00:08:57.970
you can see here in this highly detailed breakdown.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:03.130
Its maneuverability came in part from a rotating
mechanical joint that connected the front

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:05.720
of the vehicle to the mid-section.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:11.910
As tourism increased, the larger Venterial
Environment Excursion Vehicle was developed:

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:18.450
which we know from schematics used a set of
twin counter-oriented screws for propulsion.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:24.149
These safari vessels could seat up to eight
park guests, and take them deep into the Pits

00:09:24.149 --> 00:09:26.370
with supposed safety.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:31.550
‘Supposed’ being the key word here, as
a mockup of an incident report tells us that

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:37.190
vehicles were bent, melted, crushed, dented,
or dissolved at least on some occasions.

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:41.810
...Maybe traversing the unknown depths of
a giant organism isn’t a good idea after

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:42.810
all?

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:48.160
Well, as Caver Dave might say, that’s not
the right attitude for exploring the FUNderground.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:53.430
For adventurous park guests, the opportunity
of camping on natural, unreinforced trails

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:58.000
was possible with the Interventerial Tent
— shown here in this diagram.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:02.990
Unlike traditional tents, this collapsible,
multi-sided device could endure the crushing

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:06.740
shifts and deadly wildlife of the Pit while
campers slept.

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.830
At least, most of the time…

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:14.070
When things went wrong, emergency trail phones
were one way to reach park staff.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:18.640
Called ‘lighthouses’ by seasoned hikers,
these subterranean telecommunication devices

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:20.779
were highly advanced in the 1970s.

00:10:20.779 --> 00:10:27.040
And indeed, the study of the Permian Basin
Superorganism led to numerous technological

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.579
breakthroughs…

00:10:28.579 --> 00:10:34.160
One of many lucrative results from the development
of the fictional Pit were tremendous advances

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:36.450
in the field of computer science.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:42.110
In the early 1980s, Anodyne began to release
computers made of nervous tissue taken from

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:44.660
the Permian Basin Superorganism.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:50.790
With four terabytes of organic tissue storage
memory, these machines were extremely popular.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:56.790
An even more well-known product exported from
the Mystery Flesh Pit was Amniotic Ballast

00:10:56.790 --> 00:11:02.660
— a miraculous fluid from deep within the
pit branded as VitaSalve in advertisements

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.200
such as this one.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:10.050
The product could cure various illnesses,
and was almost certainly safe to use.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:16.020
But the most notable service Anodyne offered
was access to the Mystery Flesh Pit itself.

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:21.680
Aside from hiking, tourists paid for access
to the Amniotic Thermal Springs.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:26.640
The springs had strong effects on visitors
who bathed in them, including making their

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:30.230
skin healthier and giving them a euphoric
sensation.

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:35.120
As long as they could take their mind off
the fact they were bathing in an unknown liquid.

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:39.890
The true focus of the Pit for most visitors,
however, was the Lower Visitor Center — a

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:43.710
gateway into the deep that took eight years
to construct.

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:49.950
With restrooms, a gift shop, and even restaurants,
the Lower Visitor Center was the hub of the

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:50.950
national park.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:56.230
Was it a good idea to suspend a several-ton
building on steel cables in the middle of

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:57.230
the pit?

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:00.660
Anodyne Inc soon found out…

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:05.959
At last, we’ve come to the 2007 disaster
and all that follows.

00:12:05.959 --> 00:12:13.610
On July 4th, 2007, due to Anodyne’s negligence,
something as simple as heavy rain and a faulty

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:17.800
water pump caused a section of the Pit to
flood to unsafe levels.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:23.790
The result was a catastrophe most had never
imagined: the Permian Basin Superorganism

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:25.959
began to wake up.

00:12:25.959 --> 00:12:30.779
Imagine waking up from a long nap to find
hundreds of tiny bugs had built a tiny hotel

00:12:30.779 --> 00:12:31.779
in your throat.

00:12:31.779 --> 00:12:33.810
You’d be pretty mad.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:40.050
At 9:52 PM, the lifeform began a choking response
due to the flooding, causing the entire Lower

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:44.340
Visitor Center to be crushed and swallowed
deeper into its gullet.

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:45.980
But this was just the beginning.

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:51.130
According to an incident report, the creature
then started to surface: with people living

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:56.319
all around west Texas witnessing the limbs
of the superorganism rising from the ground

00:12:56.319 --> 00:13:01.339
— the scale of which is captured in this
painting from a survivor.

00:13:01.339 --> 00:13:06.500
And then, the creature returned to its slumber,
likely lulled back to sleep by a mysterious

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:10.040
contingency measure redacted from the incident
report.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:15.240
In the wake of the disaster, Anodyne was dissolved,
and the park was officially closed to the

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:20.800
public — with people perhaps finally realizing
that hiking inside a giant creature isn’t

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.959
such a good idea after all.

00:13:22.959 --> 00:13:27.810
The author imagines that the region around
the pit has now become a ghost town, but behind

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:30.370
fences, some are still monitoring it.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:34.790
In the present of this alternate timeline,
the Permian Basin Superorganism is now kept

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:39.850
under constant surveillance, but who knows
when it might awaken once more...

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:44.209
There’s a lot more lurking in the Pit you
can read about online, and you can follow

00:13:44.209 --> 00:13:49.079
and support Trevor Roberts by using the links
in the description below, or by purchasing

00:13:49.079 --> 00:13:54.280
something from the Mystery Flesh Pit gift
shop.

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:58.740
I’m Destin from the channel EDGE.

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:01.970
I cover all sorts of topics in natural history.

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:07.280
Whether it’s the extinct beasts of times
long since past, the bizarre and sticky world

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:14.310
of the living, or the extraordinary dark places
our minds go to in the supernatural or cryptozoological.

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:18.959
If you like Curious Archive, Ben G Thomas,
Trey the Explainer, you’ll enjoy me and

00:14:18.959 --> 00:14:20.720
my content as well.

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:24.750
Follow the links to my channel in the description
and comment section below!

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.750
And as always, thanks for watching.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:31.480
If you enjoyed this entry, please lend your
